   "textLength": 844,
   "text": "The clandestine process for smuggling oil under Iran’s nose goes as follows. Supertankers are considered too vulnerable to undertake the journey through the strait, so it is often the smaller “shuttle boats” that make the perilous trip.\nThe vessels turn off their automatic identification systems to prevent detection through the waterway, which is just 21 miles wide at its narrowest point.\nMost of ",
