   "textLength": 546,
   "text": "He believes the Gulf states would have adopted the practice earlier in the war if not for the intervention of the White House.\nBy issuing assurances that the conflict would be a brief one and Iranian defiance short-lived – crushed, variously, by a decisive military victory, negotiated peace or economic warfare – it stopped the oil-rich countries improvising.\n“The White House keeps telling us that ",
