   "textLength": 1391,
   "text": "According to data firm Kpler, somewhere between 10 to 12 million barrels of oil cross the strait daily: approximately half that of pre-war volumes.\nThis varies significantly from day-to-day, however. On Sept 7, Mr Johnston said, 20 million barrels crossed the waterway, but by Sept 10, it had dropped to three.\nNevertheless, countries such as the UAE, which claims to be exporting two million barrels",
